{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1546354-playable-venator-family-example","id":1546354,"title":"Playable Venator family example","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-24T12:20:39-08:00","id":1546354,"title":"Playable Venator family example","content":"One of the things I enjoy about the Curseborne setting and what we've seen so far, is how 'open' it seems to be in terms of what is possible.<br /> I'm reading more of the rules and beginning to grok them a little more, slowly but surely.<br /> <br /> So, one of the things I *want* to do eventually, is come up with a Lineage that's basically a bunch of Stands/Persona users. (I think Lineage works better than family of existing Lineage because of just how different Stands and Personas are from all the present Lineages)<br /> <br /> I'm not confident enough to try something like that just yet... So I decided to try something a little simpler instead but also inspired by the same source material.<br /> <br /> What follows is a Venator group with sample playable rules. They have their own power stat called &quot;Mastery&quot; and their own curse dice called &quot;Breath Dice&quot; that for the most part, function similarly to Entanglement and Curse dice but are labeled differently for flavor and have a few different perks.<br /> <br /> Given their humans and *NOT* Accursed, they don't have damnations and torments, and don't suffer wicked success or cruel failures either. Given more work I'd add some more powers for them, like ones dealing with how they take care of Liminal Spaces, but I think this suffices for now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Rizumu or \u201cThe Rhythm\u201d</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>\u201cNo, that wasn\u2019t Kung Fu, it was actually Sendo-Ryu Karate and something else. Something that can hurt them, destroy them. It\u2019s known as Rizumu in the east, at least that\u2019s what my mentor told me, but we call it \u2018The Rhythm\u2019. The Rhythm of life, breathing, the sun. All of it, it\u2019s inside of you and every other human, but only some of us are capable of harnessing it. Yeah, I bet you didn\u2019t expect to be taught secret vampire killing martial arts by a black guy from Detroit, but then I didn\u2019t expect to be taught it by an Italian from New Jersey. Point is, you want to get back at them for what they did to your family, right? I can teach you how to do it. You have the potential. You can make a difference.\u201d<br /> -Will \u2018Smokey\u2019 Brown</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">An ancient anti-curse technique, The Rhythm allows the practitioner to use the very power of life itself to banish curses and strike against the Accursed directly. Rizumu takes it\u2019s name from the very precise way it\u2019s users learn to breathe. The secret to accessing this energy of life is through mastery of breath, and a Rhythm user unable to breathe, is unable to use their abilities.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The energy of the Rhythm pours off of practitioners in invisible waves around them when being gathered up, though this invisible energy of life causes effects in their surroundings. Ripples form across liquid surfaces, and plants spring into full bloom while a Rizumu user gathers the energy to them, and uses it.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Rizumu users can heal others, run across water and other surfaces that shouldn\u2019t support them, perform extraordinary feats of athleticism, and most importantly, directly destroy cursed energy. One in ten thousand people is said to be capable of learning how to use the Rhythm, though most go their whole lives unaware. Despite this, Rhythm users can be found all over the world, from temples in the Himalayan mountains, to secret gyms in Hell\u2019s Kitchen Manhattan.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Most who come to learn the techniques of Rizumu are the victims of the Accursed, most often saved or discovered by senior users who recognize the potential within them. Almost every Rhythm user combines the technique with a martial art to capitalize on the effectiveness and improve physical fitness for greater reserve of energy. There is no central authority to those who practice Rizumu, as it\u2019s simply a technique passed on from master to students who then go into the world and teach others.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The only thing all Rhythm users have in common, is being enemies of the Accursed. Most being survivors or having been close to the victims of the Accursed come in with biases against them. Some pity the Accursed and see their techniques as a way to purify and give release to the Accursed, at least in the form of death. While others gladly hunt down any and all Accursed their aware of in order to \u2018cleanse\u2019 an area.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This cell like nature for these Venators means an area might only ever have one Rizumu user in the area, but as a whole no Accursed effort from any family has been able to truly \u2018wipe them out\u2019. That single Rhythm user may be able to call on a score of others for help through their various master-student relationships as well.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Systems</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Rizumu users don\u2019t have curse dice or an Entanglement rating, though they do have something that is similar mechanically.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">In place of Entanglement, those who use The Rhythm have a \u201cMastery\u201d rating. This Mastery rating refers to how deep into the secrets of Rizumu the practitioner has gone, and how many \u2018Breath Dice\u2019 a Rizumu user can hold.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Unlike the Accursed, the Rhythm users fill their pool of breath dice quite easily and quickly. The simple act of breathing gives them access to this life force energy. By contrast to the Accursed, their abilities are not as broad or powerful, though quite effective at what they\u2019re made for.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">A Rizumu user gains 1 breath dice passively every round, as long as they are able to breathe naturally.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Outside of this, a Rizumu user can gain a number of breath dice up to their limit equal to their Stamina+Mastery in a single action by doing nothing but breathing in deeply.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Any disruption to the careful breathing of a Rizumu user prevents their passive ability to gain breath dice. If they\u2019re holding their breath, being choked, or in so much pain as to be distracted, they can only regain their breath dice from active breathing\u2026and that\u2019s only if they have clean oxygen to breathe in.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">As Rizumu is based on life force, a practitioner near death is incapable of using it. Once both injuries on Maimed are filled in, the only Rizumu action they can take is \u201cThe last gift.\u201d</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Benefits<br /> Before individual technique use, these are the benefits all users of Rizumu gain while holding breath dice.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Fast Healing<br /> Rhythm users are better able to concentrate the bodies repair methods. They heal all injuries between sessions.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Disease and Poison resistance<br /> The flowing life energy within a Rhythm user makes them hale and healthy. They gain a stacking enhancement equal to their mastery to resist all poisons and diseases.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Aging Well<br /> The effect of the Rhythm holds back the physical downsides of aging. Even in their advance years, Rizumu users are not affected by the infirmities of age. Though they can live long lives, they are not granted any extra years beyond what a human has. Reaching a venerable age is still a rarity for most Rhythm users due to their battles with the Accursed.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Final Gift<br /> When a Rhythm user knows they are dying, when they have but 1 injury level left, they can decide to impart their final bit of life energy to an ally. Giving up what\u2019s left of themselves, they transfer the energy either into a liquid medium, or by directly touching the other Rhythm user. With contact made the life energy is transferred. This causes the Final Gift user to begin to die, with no way of stopping this. However the receiver of the final gift heals all health levels, fills their Breath Pool, and if the giver had a higher Mastery rating, immediately increases their rating by 1.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Techniques</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Light Step<br /> Those who master Rizumu find the energy of life allows them to find purchase on any surface<br /> Hold 2 Breath Dice<br /> Mastery 1<br /> The user can cross liquid surfaces on foot as long as they don\u2019t stop moving. They can also run across physical objects that shouldn\u2019t be able to support their weight, like thin tree branches.<br /> Mastery 2<br /> The user can stand on any liquid as if it were solid ground. The User can climb any vertical surface no matter how sheer.<br /> Mastery 3<br /> The User can run their full movement up any vertical surface and use objects such as falling leaves to leap off of to continue movement.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Aura Barrier<br /> A crackling gold aura becomes the only armor a Rizumu user needs<br /> *None of these abilities work if the character is actually wearing armor*<br /> Mastery 1<br /> Expel 1 breath dice, your body is considered to have the \u2018fitted\u2019 property for the scene.<br /> Mastery 2<br /> As above but it also now gains the \u2018Magic resistance\u2019 tag.<br /> Mastery 3<br /> Your Aura is now considered to be padded as well. Expel an additional breath dice for the effect twice.<br /> Mastery 4<br /> Expel 1 more breath dice during activation, your aura armor now has the \u2018spiked\u2019 property.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Fists of Legend<br /> A Rizumu user learns to channel their life energy into their body or the weapons they\u2019re using when making attacks. The effect causes audible vibrations in the air as well as crackling energy to encircle their fist, foot or weapon being used.<br /> Mastery 1<br /> For every breath die Expelled apply any of the following tags to your attack: Brutal, Piercing, Reach<br /> Mastery 2<br /> As above but add Wrecking, Flaming, Painful<br /> Mastery 3<br /> As above but add Poisoned, Elemental Attunement<br /> Mastery 4<br /> As above but add Deadly</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Disrupt Curse Energy<br /> With the Rhythm of life, the user forces that energy into an Accursed being, causing a variety of different effects, this requires the user to touch the target. This can be part of an attack.<br /> Mastery 1<br /> Every 2 breath dice expelled bleeds 1 curse dice from the target.<br /> Mastery 2<br /> Expel 1 breath dice for every 1 status effect placed on you from Accursed spells to end it.<br /> Mastery 3<br /> Expel 3 breath dice. You create a field of anti-curse energy surrounding the area. All Accursed spells suffer a moderate complication to activate for the rest of the scene.<br /> Mastery 4<br /> Expel 4 breath dice. You must touch the target, and this can be part of an attack. Roll Medicine+Mastery with a difficulty equal to the Accursed\u2019s Entanglement rating. If successful you turn the Accursed back into a Human for the scene. Dead become living and breathing in whatever body they\u2019ve taken, Primals drop out of their Wild form, Hungry cannot access undead might. The Accursed remains human for the entire scene. If they die while human, their soul passes on to the hereafter.</span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}